<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Northern Bakeries interim shr inches higher.</title>
<headline>Northern Bakeries interim shr inches higher.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended March 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, (cts)		4.94	  vs  4.18</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 1.50	  vs  1.00</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   2.82	  vs  2.39</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   5.54	  vs  3.75</p>
<p>    Tax			 2.68	  vs  1.41</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   1.95	  vs  1.08</p>
<p>    Turnover		  136.40	vs  109.24</p>
<p>Div payable July 25</p>
<p>on register July 4</p>
<p>Full name: Northern Bakeries Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said capital expenditure of 5.2 million rand had been approved for the current year.</p>
<p>It said it was confident that the positive trend would be repeated in the next six months and that earnings will be higher than expected.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
